// Tenant provisioning manifest produced by the AI agent for a single new org.
//
// What the AI actually decides (the ONLY mutable surface):
//   1. `tenant.*`                  — company name, industry, locale, timezone, etc.
//   2. `hr_hub.employees[]`        — per-employee: position, team, department,
//                                    job_title, job_type, job_level.
//   3. `tickets.queues[]`          — JUST the list of queue IDs to show.
//   4. `projects.projects[]`       — JUST the list of project IDs to show.
//   5. `dashboard.dashboards[]`    — JUST the list of dashboard IDs to show.
//   6. `kpi.kpis[]`                — JUST the list of KPI IDs to show.
//   7. `hr_hub.request_types[]`    — JUST the list of HR request type IDs to show.
//
// Everything else is FROZEN. Queue assignment (icon, email, members, managers,
// allowed_categories), project leads/teams/start dates, dashboard widgets and
// their KPI bindings, etc. are pre-configured in the static catalog and applied
// automatically when an ID is included. The right employees come pre-attached
// to the right queues/projects through the catalog.
//
// `name` fields next to IDs exist only so a human reviewing this JSON knows what
// the ID refers to. They are frozen and ignored by the provisioning service.
// Tickets are NOT listed: they travel with their queue from the catalog.

